[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66002,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid sarcoma is a malignant mesenchymal neoplasm that exhibits partial or complete epithelioid cytomorphology and immunophenotype. Two clinicopathological subtypes are recognized: the classic (or distal) form is characterized by its proclivity for acral sites and pseudogranulomatous growth pattern; the proximal-type (large cell) subtype arises mainly in proximal/truncal regions, and it consists of nests and sheets of large epithelioid cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66003,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8804/3 Epithelioid sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66004,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5F.2 &amp; XH4F96 Sarcoma, not elsewhere classified of other specified sites &amp; Epithelioid sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66005,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66006,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Classic epithelioid sarcoma (also known as conventional or distal epithelioid sarcoma); proximal or large cell epithelioid sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66007,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Within the female genital tract, the vulva is the most common location.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66008,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with a rapidly growing mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66009,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epithelioid sarcoma is uncommon, with most tumours involving the vulva being of the proximal type. The patient age range is wide, but there is a peak in the fourth to fifth decade of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66010,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66011,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Loss of expression of SMARCB1 (INI1), part of the SWI/SNF complex, is a unifying feature and probably the earliest genetic event in these tumours. Epithelioid sarcoma can have complex karyotypes. Beyond the loss of SMARCB1 (INI1), the pathogenesis of this entity is largely unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66012,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours usually measure &lt;&nbsp;6&nbsp;cm and typically have a greyish-white cut surface that may be multinodular. Haemorrhage and/or necrosis may be present {25651469}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66013,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Classic epithelioid sarcoma consists of cellular nodules of epithelioid and spindled tumour cells with central degeneration and/or necrosis&nbsp;&ndash; a growth pattern that imparts a vaguely granulomatous appearance to the process {3717528}. Fusion of necrotizing nodules results in a serpiginous mass with central geographical necrosis. The proximal type may have a diffuse or multinodular growth pattern, with common involvement of subcutaneous and deep soft tissue. In the vulva, most cases are of proximal type and neoplastic cells are large, with abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm and eccentric nuclei with vesicular nuclei and prominent nucleoli. Rhabdoid inclusions are common. Myxoid stroma may be focally present or (in rare cases) dominant.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemically, the tumour cells are positive for keratin, EMA, and vimentin and show loss of SMARCB1 (INI1) expression {9042279; 19033866; 26645461; 25651469}. Approximately half stain for CD34, and tumour cells may occasionally be positive for actin and desmin. Additionally, rare cases of epithelioid sarcoma demonstrate hybrid histological features of both classic and proximal types.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66014,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66015,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66016,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> diffuse or nodular growth of epithelioid cells with abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm; some degree of EMA or keratin positivity and loss of SMARCB1 (INI1) expression.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> CD34 expression, generally focal.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-07T17:28:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66017,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging is similar to that for other sarcomas of the trunk and extremities.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66018,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 441,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Proximal-type epithelioid sarcoma acts more aggressively than the conventional (distal) type of epithelioid sarcoma, with more frequent recurrences and a higher incidence of metastasis {11454997; 25663591}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:36:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]